{"id":"thyroid","cards":[{"id":"thyroidfc7dd9f","l":1,"f":"<b>Two cell types, two different cancers</b>?","b":"<b>follicular cells</b> make T3/T4 and keep iodine uptake/TSH response (→ RAI works); <b>parafollicular C cells</b> (ultimobranchial body) make <b>calcitonin</b> → <b>medullary carcinoma</b>, which does <b>not</b> respond to RAI.","c":"Core concept"},{"id":"thyroi99b23bed","l":2,"f":"Thyroid neoplasm from the <b>parafollicular C cells</b>","b":"<b>medullary carcinoma</b>","c":"Core concept"},{"id":"thyroi8bb2ca2d","l":1,"f":"<b>Thyroglossal duct cyst</b>?","b":"midline neck mass, often in childhood, may get infected; <b>moves with swallowing AND with tongue protrusion</b> — always test both.","c":"Embryology"},{"id":"thyroidc69c0d4","l":2,"f":"12-year-old girl, midline neck mass moving with swallowing and tongue protrusion","b":"<b>Sistrunk procedure</b> (cyst + tract + middle third of the hyoid)","c":"Embryology"},{"id":"thyroi95c86348","l":1,"f":"<b>Lingual/ectopic thyroid</b>?","b":"failure of descent; can obstruct the airway. <b>Before removing it, confirm a normally placed cervical thyroid (US)</b> — it may be the only thyroid tissue.","c":"Embryology"},{"id":"thyroi5697ebf0","l":1,"f":"<b>Superior thyroid</b> — Origin?","b":"<b>External carotid</b>","c":"Anatomy"},{"id":"thyroi687725b1","l":1,"f":"<b>Inferior thyroid</b> — Origin?","b":"<b>Thyrocervical trunk</b> (subclavian)","c":"Anatomy"},{"id":"thyroi234620ec","l":1,"f":"<b>Thyroid ima (inconstant)</b> — Origin?","b":"Brachiocephalic trunk / aortic arch","c":"Anatomy"},{"id":"thyroif255e7c4","l":1,"f":"<b>Superior &amp; middle thyroid</b> — Drains to?","b":"Internal jugular","c":"Anatomy"},{"id":"thyroia4d846f4","l":1,"f":"<b>Inferior thyroid</b> — Drains to?","b":"Brachiocephalic","c":"Anatomy"},{"id":"thyroibc343a84","l":2,"f":"Nerves at risk in thyroidectomy","b":"<b>recurrent laryngeal + external branch of the superior laryngeal nerve</b>","c":"Anatomy"},{"id":"thyroi0c6c8f94","l":2,"f":"Mechanism that <b>lowers</b> plasma calcium","b":"<b>calcitonin acting on the kidneys</b> (↑ calcium excretion) — PTH and vitamin D raise calcium","c":"Physiology"},{"id":"thyroi9cd8c25b","l":1,"f":"<b>Ultrasound</b> — Role?","b":"Standard first-line thyroid imaging","c":"Evaluation"},{"id":"thyroi14560e97","l":1,"f":"<b>Imaging CT</b> — Role?","b":"Selective: <b>retrosternal extension</b>, invasion, deep/mediastinal disease, node mapping","c":"Evaluation"},{"id":"thyroi3c79276c","l":1,"f":"<b>Uptake scan</b> — Role?","b":"Function, not morphology — for hyperthyroid states, not cancer diagnosis","c":"Evaluation"},{"id":"thyroi96ac1b55","l":2,"f":"Cough + mild dysphagia, enlarged right lobe → <b>CT neck and chest</b> (retrosternal extension) ; neck mass moving with swallowing + dyspnoea and dysphagia","b":"<b>retrosternal thyroid</b>","c":"Evaluation"},{"id":"thyroi4baf32a8","l":1,"f":"<b>Hypothyroidism alone is NOT an indication for surgery</b>?","b":"only with another indication (compressive goitre, suspicious nodule).","c":"Hypo- & hyperthyroidism"},{"id":"thyroib9c5d5b7","l":2,"f":"Hypothyroid patient for elective lap chole","b":"<b>postpone until euthyroid</b> ; hypothyroid patients risk <b>myxoedema coma</b> after surgery","c":"Hypo- & hyperthyroidism"},{"id":"thyroi43533f9b","l":1,"f":"<b>Graves</b>?","b":"autoimmune, diffuse; stimulating antibodies. <b>Ophthalmopathy</b> worsens with smoking and with <b>RAI</b> → significant eye disease favours <b>thyroidectomy</b>.","c":"Hypo- & hyperthyroidism"},{"id":"thyroi6a152f99","l":2,"f":"Woman of childbearing age with a <b>hot (toxic) nodule</b>","b":"keyed <b>antithyroid medication</b> (RAI avoided if planning pregnancy; lobectomy is the definitive option)","c":"Hypo- & hyperthyroidism"},{"id":"thyroi30dddcd8","l":1,"f":"<b>Acute suppurative</b> — Features?","b":"Rare bacterial, pus; painful swelling, fever; US collection","c":"Thyroiditis"},{"id":"thyroi6bc3ea7c","l":1,"f":"<b>Acute suppurative</b> — Management?","b":"Infection treatment + <b>drainage</b>","c":"Thyroiditis"},{"id":"thyroi30a44274","l":1,"f":"<b>Subacute (de Quervain)</b> — Features?","b":"Painful, non-suppurative; tender; no collection","c":"Thyroiditis"},{"id":"thyroi5a757d6d","l":1,"f":"<b>Subacute (de Quervain)</b> — Management?","b":"Self-limited, no surgery","c":"Thyroiditis"},{"id":"thyroi1fc93355","l":1,"f":"<b>Hashimoto</b> — Features?","b":"Autoimmune → hypothyroidism; goitre; anti-TPO/anti-thyroglobulin","c":"Thyroiditis"},{"id":"thyroib52b120a","l":1,"f":"<b>Hashimoto</b> — Management?","b":"Surgery only for large/compressive gland or suspicious lesion","c":"Thyroiditis"},{"id":"thyroi7ba4063c","l":1,"f":"<b>Riedel</b> — Features?","b":"Extensive fibrosis, constricts structures","c":"Thyroiditis"},{"id":"thyroie09194b3","l":1,"f":"<b>Riedel</b> — Management?","b":"Surgery for compression","c":"Thyroiditis"},{"id":"thyroi2feca0e8","l":2,"f":"Long-standing <b>Hashimoto's</b> + rapidly enlarging diffuse goitre with stridor","b":"<b>thyroid lymphoma</b>","c":"Thyroiditis"},{"id":"thyroid747dfe8","l":2,"f":"Solitary nodule, normal TFTs, suspicious US","b":"<b>FNA cytology</b>","c":"Thyroid nodule & goitre"},{"id":"thyroi64e0edd8","l":1,"f":"<b>Bethesda I</b> — Meaning?","b":"Non-diagnostic","c":"Thyroid nodule & goitre"},{"id":"thyroi4d292eaf","l":1,"f":"<b>Bethesda I</b> — Malignancy risk?","b":"~1–4%","c":"Thyroid nodule & goitre"},{"id":"thyroice36915c","l":1,"f":"<b>Bethesda I</b> — Management?","b":"<b>Repeat US-guided FNA</b>","c":"Thyroid nodule & goitre"},{"id":"thyroibff5a4fc","l":1,"f":"<b>Bethesda II</b> — Meaning?","b":"<b>Benign</b>","c":"Thyroid nodule & goitre"},{"id":"thyroibb05df21","l":1,"f":"<b>Bethesda II</b> — Malignancy risk?","b":"~3%","c":"Thyroid nodule & goitre"},{"id":"thyroi2cf87675","l":1,"f":"<b>Bethesda II</b> — Management?","b":"Surveillance; surgery only for another indication (compression)","c":"Thyroid nodule & goitre"},{"id":"thyroid3ea55ac","l":1,"f":"<b>Bethesda III</b> — Meaning?","b":"AUS/FLUS","c":"Thyroid nodule & goitre"},{"id":"thyroie797ec9b","l":1,"f":"<b>Bethesda III</b> — Malignancy risk?","b":"Intermediate","c":"Thyroid nodule & goitre"},{"id":"thyroidc569f6c","l":1,"f":"<b>Bethesda III</b> — Management?","b":"Repeat / further work-up","c":"Thyroid nodule & goitre"},{"id":"thyroidf339efc","l":1,"f":"<b>Bethesda IV</b> — Meaning?","b":"Follicular neoplasm","c":"Thyroid nodule & goitre"},{"id":"thyroie18c75b1","l":1,"f":"<b>Bethesda IV</b> — Malignancy risk?","b":"~15–30%","c":"Thyroid nodule & goitre"},{"id":"thyroi4dce78d0","l":1,"f":"<b>Bethesda IV</b> — Management?","b":"Molecular testing or <b>diagnostic lobectomy</b>","c":"Thyroid nodule & goitre"},{"id":"thyroi09992760","l":1,"f":"<b>Bethesda V</b> — Meaning?","b":"Suspicious for malignancy","c":"Thyroid nodule & goitre"},{"id":"thyroi0eb9b363","l":1,"f":"<b>Bethesda V</b> — Malignancy risk?","b":"High","c":"Thyroid nodule & goitre"},{"id":"thyroib6561abd","l":1,"f":"<b>Bethesda V</b> — Management?","b":"Surgery","c":"Thyroid nodule & goitre"},{"id":"thyroiddc67d3f","l":1,"f":"<b>Bethesda VI</b> — Meaning?","b":"Malignant","c":"Thyroid nodule & goitre"},{"id":"thyroi01e2669f","l":1,"f":"<b>Bethesda VI</b> — Management?","b":"By cancer type","c":"Thyroid nodule & goitre"},{"id":"thyroi4221deff","l":2,"f":"3-cm <b>benign (Bethesda II)</b> nodule with a <b>choking sensation</b>","b":"<b>hemithyroidectomy</b> (compressive symptoms)","c":"Thyroid nodule & goitre"},{"id":"thyroic03cd5ad","l":1,"f":"<b>Papillary</b> — Frequency?","b":"<b>~85%</b>","c":"Thyroid cancer"},{"id":"thyroi247a2ad2","l":1,"f":"<b>Follicular</b> — Frequency?","b":"~10%","c":"Thyroid cancer"},{"id":"thyroi90195b4e","l":1,"f":"<b>Medullary</b> — Frequency?","b":"Uncommon","c":"Thyroid cancer"},{"id":"thyroie6c0daf1","l":1,"f":"<b>Anaplastic</b> — Frequency?","b":"<b>~1%</b>","c":"Thyroid cancer"},{"id":"thyroiab96061d","l":1,"f":"<b>Papillary</b> — Who?","b":"Younger adults","c":"Thyroid cancer"},{"id":"thyroi7efe95b3","l":1,"f":"<b>Follicular</b> — Who?","b":"≥ 40","c":"Thyroid cancer"},{"id":"thyroi9b683a2e","l":1,"f":"<b>Medullary</b> — Who?","b":"~25% familial (<b>MEN 2, RET</b>)","c":"Thyroid cancer"},{"id":"thyroi529bbf8a","l":1,"f":"<b>Anaplastic</b> — Who?","b":"Elderly women (60s–70s)","c":"Thyroid cancer"},{"id":"thyroicb2db0b0","l":1,"f":"<b>Papillary</b> — Spread?","b":"<b>Lymphatic</b> (nodes common)","c":"Thyroid cancer"},{"id":"thyroib111380c","l":1,"f":"<b>Follicular</b> — Spread?","b":"<b>Haematogenous</b> (vascular invasion)","c":"Thyroid cancer"},{"id":"thyroi1d165495","l":1,"f":"<b>Medullary</b> — Spread?","b":"Nodes","c":"Thyroid cancer"},{"id":"thyroi2bfbad69","l":1,"f":"<b>Anaplastic</b> — Spread?","b":"Early local invasion, metastases","c":"Thyroid cancer"},{"id":"thyroic8d150ca","l":1,"f":"<b>Papillary</b> — Key point?","b":"BRAF; variants (tall cell, diffuse sclerosing); NIFTP","c":"Thyroid cancer"},{"id":"thyroid9e18785","l":1,"f":"<b>Follicular</b> — Key point?","b":"FNA can't tell adenoma from carcinoma — needs <b>capsular/vascular invasion</b> on histology","c":"Thyroid cancer"},{"id":"thyroib7fcb0c8","l":1,"f":"<b>Medullary</b> — Key point?","b":"<b>Calcitonin, CEA</b>; no RAI","c":"Thyroid cancer"},{"id":"thyroi4001e626","l":1,"f":"<b>Anaplastic</b> — Key point?","b":"All <b>stage IV</b>; palliative; survival &gt; 2 y uncommon","c":"Thyroid cancer"},{"id":"thyroi9bdaf2fc","l":1,"f":"<b>Papillary</b> — Prognosis?","b":"~96%","c":"Thyroid cancer"},{"id":"thyroi62c1f4bc","l":1,"f":"<b>Follicular</b> — Prognosis?","b":"Very good","c":"Thyroid cancer"},{"id":"thyroifcd85dc7","l":1,"f":"<b>Medullary</b> — Prognosis?","b":"Worse","c":"Thyroid cancer"},{"id":"thyroi9e2b8356","l":1,"f":"<b>Anaplastic</b> — Prognosis?","b":"Very poor","c":"Thyroid cancer"},{"id":"thyroi24873631","l":2,"f":"Enlarged cervical nodes with a <b>normal thyroid</b> on exam in a 33-year-old","b":"<b>papillary</b> carcinoma","c":"Thyroid cancer"},{"id":"thyroib348f596","l":2,"f":"New name for the encapsulated (non-invasive) follicular variant of PTC","b":"<b>NIFTP</b>","c":"Thyroid cancer"},{"id":"thyroi90bce48e","l":2,"f":"Pre-treatment diagnostic marker (keyed)","b":"<b>calcitonin</b> (medullary)","c":"Thyroid cancer"},{"id":"thyroi667dd9c2","l":1,"f":"<b>Treatment: total thyroidectomy + central (level VI) neck dissection</b>?","b":"never a partial procedure; add lateral dissection when lateral nodes are involved.","c":"Thyroid cancer › Medullary carcinoma & MEN 2"},{"id":"thyroibafdca07","l":2,"f":"Medullary carcinoma, 0.5-cm left nodule with enlarged left neck nodes","b":"keyed <b>total thyroidectomy + central neck dissection</b> (the source notes ipsilateral lateral dissection is also needed — key follows the doctor)","c":"Thyroid cancer › Medullary carcinoma & MEN 2"},{"id":"thyroi0b3a4597","l":1,"f":"<b>&lt; 1 cm (microcarcinoma)</b> — Extent?","b":"Lobectomy possible","c":"Thyroid cancer › Treating differentiated cancer"},{"id":"thyroic79bc3c5","l":1,"f":"<b>1–4 cm</b> — Extent?","b":"Lobectomy <b>or</b> total thyroidectomy by risk","c":"Thyroid cancer › Treating differentiated cancer"},{"id":"thyroi67946ca5","l":1,"f":"<b>&gt; 4 cm</b> — Extent?","b":"<b>Total thyroidectomy</b> (RAI needs all thyroid removed)","c":"Thyroid cancer › Treating differentiated cancer"},{"id":"thyroi7628686f","l":1,"f":"<b>TSH suppression</b>?","b":"levothyroxine at <b>suppressive</b> doses (not just replacement) — dose guided by TSH/free T4.","c":"Thyroid cancer › Treating differentiated cancer"},{"id":"thyroi116bd57a","l":1,"f":"<b>Thyroglobulin</b>?","b":"tumour marker after total thyroidectomy ± RAI: a rising Tg = residual/recurrent disease (check anti-Tg antibodies). MTC follow-up = <b>calcitonin + CEA</b>.","c":"Thyroid cancer › Treating differentiated cancer"},{"id":"thyroi939b28fe","l":2,"f":"Papillary cancer, long-standing swelling, euthyroid","b":"keyed <b>hemithyroidectomy</b>","c":"Thyroid cancer › Treating differentiated cancer"},{"id":"thyroi55cb04c1","l":2,"f":"Expanding <b>neck haematoma</b> with stridor 2 h post-op → <b>open the wound and evacuate at the bedside</b> ; the most serious immediate complication in Graves'","b":"<b>neck haematoma</b>","c":"Complications of thyroidectomy"},{"id":"thyroif0681a94","l":2,"f":"Perioral tingling, cramps, Chvostek's → <b>hypocalcaemia</b> ; treat with <b>IV calcium gluconate</b> ; first action (keyed) → <b>order a calcium level</b> ; numb fingers 2 weeks later","b":"<b>Chvostek's sign</b> ; labs keyed <b>low Ca, low PTH</b> (phosphate actually rises)","c":"Complications of thyroidectomy"},{"id":"thyroi9e1fc4b1","l":2,"f":"True statement about thyroidectomy risks","b":"<b>a parathyroid can be autografted</b> (into the forearm or sternomastoid); bleeding is uncommon and neuropraxia is commoner than permanent nerve injury","c":"Complications of thyroidectomy"},{"id":"thyroidc88510b","l":2,"f":"Elderly woman, 2-year swelling <b>behind the mandible</b> (parotid)","b":"<b>FNA</b>","c":"Other neck swellings (from past exams)"},{"id":"thyroi39a403e7","l":2,"f":"Lateral neck mass with <b>fever and sweating</b>","b":"<b>TB work-up (PPD)</b>","c":"Other neck swellings (from past exams)"},{"id":"thyroi2bd7b452","l":2,"f":"Swelling under the mandible, palpable in the mouth, <b>pain on eating</b>","b":"<b>submandibular gland stone</b>","c":"Other neck swellings (from past exams)"},{"id":"thyroi2f6e5a05","l":2,"f":"Posterior triangle — posterior border","b":"<b>trapezius</b> (anterior border sternocleidomastoid, base the clavicle)","c":"Other neck swellings (from past exams)"}]}